s/cpp/build/arm64-exception-handling)"," ","+On ARM64, the `pac` unwind opcode strips pointer authentication bits from `Lr` using the target's [PlatformMetadata](./PlatformMetadata.md) pointer-authentication mask before `Lr` is copied to `Pc`. The same mask is applied to return addresses recovered from explicit Frames, both when reporting the return address and when updating the context's instruction pointer.  Since pointer authentication keys are not available via the data contract, return addresses cannot be authenticated.","+"," <!-- BEGIN GENERATED: usage contract=StackWalk version=c1 -->"," ### Data descriptors used"," "],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/design/datacontracts/data-descriptor-meanings.json","lines":["@@ -468,6 +468,7 @@","     \"PInvokeCalliFrame.VASigCookiePtr\": \"Pointer to the varargs signature cookie for the unmanaged call\",","     \"PInvokeMethodDesc.Size\": \"Base size for mcPInvoke classification\",","     \"PlatformMetadata.CodePointerFlags\": \"fields describing the behavior of target code pointers\",","+    \"PlatformMetadata.PointerAuthenticationMask\": \"Bits to clear from pointer-authenticated return addresses\",","     \"PlatformMetadata.PrecodeMachineDescriptor\": \"precode stub-related platform specific properties\",","     \"PortableEntryPoint.ActualCode\": \"Native code for the entrypoint; on WebAssembly R2R code this is a function-table index (only defined if `FeaturePortableEntrypoints` is enabled)\",","     \"PortableEntryPoint.Flags\": \"Portable entrypoint flags; `0x4` means the interpreter entrypoint is preferred over `ActualCode` (only defined if `FeaturePortableEntrypoints` is enabled)\","],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/coreclr/unwinder/arm64/unwinder.cpp","lines":["@@ -346,7 +346,12 @@ Return Value:"," --*/"," {","     UNREFERENCED_PARAMETER(Sp);","+#if defined(TARGET_UNIX)","     *Pointer &= 0x0000FFFFFFFFFFFF;","+#else","+    // Windows uses 47-bit user addre